# Frappe Bench Commands

Run bench commands directly in the terminal. Do **not** tell the user to run them unless the command requires their approval or credentials you cannot use.

## Bench root

```text
/home/lovemore/frappe-bench
```

## Default site

Use `maita` unless the user specifies another site.

## When to run what

| Change type | Command |
|---|---|
| DocType JSON / patches / new fields | `bench --site maita migrate` |
| Python, JS, hooks, or integration code | `bench restart` |
| Doctype + code in same task | `migrate` then `restart` |
| One-off scripts / validation | `bench --site maita execute <module.path>` |
| Clear cache if behaviour still stale | `bench --site maita clear-cache` |

## Order of operations

1. Make code changes
2. `bench --site maita migrate` (if doctypes or patches changed)
3. `bench restart` (after backend/frontend code changes)
4. Verify with `bench --site maita execute ...` when a test script exists

## Examples

```bash
cd /home/lovemore/frappe-bench && bench --site maita migrate
cd /home/lovemore/frappe-bench && bench restart
cd /home/lovemore/frappe-bench && bench --site maita execute freightmas.integrations.tracking.test_traqo_sandbox.run
```

Request `all` permissions when supervisor restart needs it.
